TYPE ERROR: Foreign declaration 'netSend' redeclares a built-in runtime name with a NARROWER effect row on the result of argument 2 of 2: the built-in performs <Net "a.com/*">, this declaration claims <Net "b.com/*">, which does not cover <Net "a.com/*">. A local extern whose name matches a stdlib/runtime.mdk built-in is always lowered as that built-in, whatever the local signature says — so 'netSend' really does perform <Net "a.com/*">, and every caller typechecked against this declaration would be told it does not. Declare the built-in's own row `<Net "a.com/*">` (a WIDER row such as `<IO>` is also accepted — over-declaring is safe), or rename the extern to a name the runtime does not already define
